      "writtenOn": "2023-01-09T15:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This works but feels convoluted as the point of preferring `\u0026[]` in an API over `Vec` is to move the \"`Vec`-ness\" of the code to the caller (so that the resulting code only relies on `Vec` iff the caller wants it) but here you embed it within the function. Furthermore, not exposing `CStr` in the API adds an implicit requirement that the compiler can\u0027t reason about, which then can make the program `panic` within the `.map`, making it potentially a pain to debug (as the line number won\u0027t point to the data).\n\nTo avoid unnecessary intermediate conversions (`\u0026[]`-to-`Vec`-to`\u0026[]` or `\u0026[u8]`-to-`CStr`-to-`\u0026[u8]`) while still encapsulating the NULL-endianness, would it make sense for `verify_partitions` to take a `\u0026[\u0026CStr]` (so that the compiler can reason about the strings being valid) and populate an internal array of size `MAX_NUMBER_OF_VBMETA_IMAGES` with the pointers, followed by the NULL pointer?\n\nBTW, in the caller, you can take the slice from an array instead of doing the extra work of declaring a `vec!`.",
      "parentUuid": "e2d81931_0b3654c9",
