      "writtenOn": "2023-01-09T15:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e `verify_payload` will handle the logic the logic around whether payload has initrd or not.\n\nAck; that makes sense.\n\n\u003e If we try to read the partition `initrd` when it is empty, an error will be raised in `read_from_partition`.\n\nYes but it would improve error logging to have that error reflect the different cases i.e. to have `read_from_partition(\"initrd\")` return \n\n- `AVB_IO_RESULT_ERROR_NO_SUCH_PARTITION` when `initrd\u003d\u003dNone`\n- `AVB_IO_RESULT_ERROR_RANGE_OUTSIDE_PARTITION` when `initrd\u003d\u003dSome(\u0026[])`\n\nwhich requires keeping track of the `Option`, no?",
