      "writtenOn": "2023-01-06T15:26:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In terms of encapsulation, as `Payload` is already aware of what \"partitions\"/slices it has, would it make sense to make `verify_partitions` take no argument and implement `verify_payload` as\n```\n{\n    let payload \u003d Payload {...};\n    payload.verify()\n}\n```\n?",
