      "writtenOn": "2023-01-06T15:26:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that most people won\u0027t be aware of what a hash descriptor is; could this (and related variables and file) be renamed `kernel_without_initrd`/`kernel_with_no_initrd`/`kernel_alone`/... or am I misinterpreting what the single hash descriptor represents?\n\nThe test referred to by the `TODO` below could then be called `payload_missing_initrd_`[`_normal_`]`fails_verification` (for example).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 432,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 432,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "734a93c72788de6ec36f161b55ba096a239b6ad6",
