    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b43cb2e3_b57a2207",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 432,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-09T13:22:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I mean the hash descriptors in kernel\u0027s footer. I want to test the spec that given no initrd,\n\n1. if the kernel footer has only one hash descriptor \u003d\u003e pass\n2. if the kernel footer has more than one hash descriptor \u003d\u003e fail\n\nThe name `kernel_without_initrd/kernel_with_no_initrd/kernel_alone` doesn\u0027t really distinguish the two scenarios above as both 1. and 2. are `kernel_without_initrd`. I\u0027m open to take a different set of names here, but I\u0027d like to have two names that could reveal the similarities/difference between them.",
      "parentUuid": "b0399f39_148d9be2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 432,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 432,
        "endChar": 45
      },
