      "lineNbr": 432,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-09T15:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, we agree and picking good names isn\u0027t easy. Here, we need a name that isn\u0027t confusing due to requiring unnecessary extra knowledge but that also clearly differs from other tests.\n\nOverall, my point is that, if a test fails, the test name should immediately give a clear idea of what the test is covering and `with_one_hashdesc` goes against that IMO because it requires low-level/niche knowledge and still doesn\u0027t fully describe the test as the hash descriptor, beyond being unique in the VBMeta, could describe something else than the kernel (in particular when we\u0027ll expand to `with_three_hashdesc`), be invalid, ...\n\nDo you think the following names are too close:\n\n- `payload_with_no_initrd_passes_verification` for a kernel having been signed with no extra hash descriptor\n- `payload_missing_initrd_fails_verification` for a kernel having been signed with `initrd` hash(es), where no `initrd` is loaded\n\n? Because we\u0027ll also need tests for\n\n- `payload_with_unexpected_initrd_fails_verification` for the first case but where the test still loads an initrd\n- `payload_with_invalid_initrd_fails_verification` for the second case where the test loads a corrupted initrd\n- `payload_with_valid_initrd_passes_verification`\n- `payload_with_valid_initrd_debug_passes_verification`\n\nso we need an extensible naming format and I suppose what I\u0027m suggesting is\n```\npayload_(with_(valid|invalid|no)|missing)_(initrd|initrd_debug)_(passes|fails)_verification\n```\n\nhaving this sort of convention will also help with ensuring that we have exhaustive coverage of the test cases.",
      "parentUuid": "b43cb2e3_b57a2207",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 432,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 432,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "734a93c72788de6ec36f161b55ba096a239b6ad6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ce5fd18_343aaf02",
