        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-09T16:37:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that we need the four tests you mentioned (or maybe more) about `initrd \u003d Some()` case, but the problem we are discussing is about `initrd \u003d None`. I only want to distinguish when `initrd \u003d None`, footer has one hashdesc or two hashdescs.\n\n\u003e my point is that, if a test fails, the test name should immediately give a clear idea of what the test is covering \n\nI agree. TBH, I don\u0027t think I can tell the difference between `payload_with_no_initrd` and `payload_missing_initrd` without your comments after them. It\u0027s not clear whether `initrd` here means data or the hashdesc in footer? Why when initrd is in footer we use `missing`, for the other we use `with no`?\n\nHaving a united naming format is nice, but we cannot sacrifice the clarity for it.",
      "parentUuid": "f4566bec_ebd04465",
